From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:01:49 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: apple: Move the lid-following microphone jack into its
 own module

Closing the lid of an Apple silicon MacBook disconnects its internal
microphones in hardware. The T8140 AOP audio driver follows the lid
switches through the input core and reports an "Internal Mic" jack that
reads unplugged while a lid is closed. The other AOP microphone cards
need the same, so move it out of the driver into aop_lid.rs.

MicLid keeps the lid bookkeeping, the input handler and the jack report
work, unchanged, and owns its own reference count, so a driver only holds
an Arc<MicLid>, attaches it to its card before registering the card and
detaches it before freeing the card. The handler's private data is now
the MicLid instead of the T8140 driver data.

No functional change for the T8140 card. The lid KUnit suite moves with
the code as snd_soc_apple_aop_lid.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 454c2697e2dc9c97bb57f93ae380fac7cefa0218)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
